# L §5.7 Parts and lifespans (2.1-C7b-8): "a death's posting reads the place, so it runs after every movement that
# changes the place that day and doesn't depend on it (§5.14.2), and a part labelled to the party by a movement after
# the posting that day is one it holds at the close, so that part's place is refused from that day on (RUN-LIFESPAN,
# <party> ends on <d> holding parts of <place>; ENGINE.md §4.2 step 5)".  tomek dies on 2026-03-10; death_sav relabels
# his parts to his estate; final_pay, `after death_sav` (its when reads his part, now 0), pays his last wage into sav labelled his.  q: sav before the
# day is known; from 2026-03-10 it is refused.  (The probe writer's p24, writer 11's third round.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-06-30

source src "s"
unit DUK: currency minor 0.01
kind estates: parties
kind persons: parties
kind deaths: event certain
  leg what: any
  attr deceased: key persons
  attr estate: key estates
kind inheritances: transfers
  attr heir: key parties
kind wages_in: transfers
  attr employee: key persons
kind savings: place DUK min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(DUK)
  takes k for w order (if w in deaths and k.owner == w.deceased then 0 else 1)
place sav: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place employer: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input rows: observed
input death_day: date
input who_died: key persons
input estate_of: key estates
input wage: money DUK
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule inherited = (if p == m.heir then 1 else 0) when m in inheritances
  rule to_estate = (if p == m.estate then 1 else 0) when m in deaths
  rule paid = (if p == m.employee then 1 else 0) when m in wages_in

move death_sav: deaths
  on death_day
  at death_day
  reads sav
  attr deceased = who_died
  attr estate = estate_of
  leg what from sav to sav amount bal(sav) of who_died

move final_pay: wages_in
  on death_day
  at death_day
  when bal(sav) of who_died == 0 DUK
  reads sav
  after death_sav
  attr employee = who_died
  leg cash from employer to sav amount wage

ask q: bal(sav, 2026-03-09) of tomek, bal(sav, 2026-03-10), bal(sav, 2026-03-31) of tomek_estate

version cast
  cite src
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1988-04-12..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1986-09-03..2026-03-10
  estates + [tomek_estate] lives 2026-03-10..

version recs
  cite src
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[sav] = 0 at 2026-01-01 start
  death_day = 2026-03-10
  who_died = tomek
  estate_of = tomek_estate
  wage = 2400.00 DUK
  rows[r1] = (on: 2026-01-05, kind: inheritances, leg cash from world to sav amount 7000.00 DUK, heir: tomek) "line 1"
=== expect
q: (7 000.00 DUK, refused: RUN-LIFESPAN tomek ends on 2026-03-10 holding parts of sav, refused: RUN-LIFESPAN tomek ends on 2026-03-10 holding parts of sav)
...
